# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Media binaries -- never commit these.
#
# Two distinct reasons, and the first one is not negotiable:
#
# 1. COPYRIGHTED REFERENCE MATERIAL. work/ref/, work/ref2/ and work/refscan/
#    hold video downloaded from YouTube with yt-dlp (ref_full.mp4, 34MB and
#    37MB, plus extracted audio and frame dumps; work/ref2 alone is 988MB).
#    This repository is PUBLIC. Committing them would redistribute someone
#    else's copyrighted video, and it violates this project's own hard
#    constraint: "No copyrighted assets" and "The reference is a benchmark,
#    not a source." They are re-downloadable from the source URL on demand, so
#    nothing is lost by leaving them out.
#
# 2. BUILD OUTPUT. Rendered video (work3/assembly/*.mp4, work3/segments/*/
#    segment.mp4) is regenerable from source with _build_segments.py and
#    _assemble.py. The .pre-* files are point-in-time backups that exist only to
#    survive a bad fix pass -- keeping them in git would add ~300MB of history
#    forever. GitHub also hard-rejects files over 100MB.
#
# Everything needed to REBUILD is committed: sources, beats.json, the plan and
# fact JSONs, and the gates. See README-rebuild.md for the fetch-then-render
# path.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.mp4
*.wav
*.mkv
*.mov
*.webm
*.m4a
*.flac
*.mp3

# Reference material explicitly, belt-and-braces in case a future download
# lands with an extension not listed above.
work/ref/
work/ref2/
work/refscan/
work/refstudy/
work3/measure/refscan/
ref_*.mp4
ref_*.wav

# REFERENCE VIDEO FRAMES, as images. The container rules above stop the .mp4/.wav
# but NOT the stills pulled out of it: work/study/ref_200.png, ref_256.png,
# ref_300.png, ref_445.png and ref_s1_*.png (12 files, ~2.5MB) are single frames
# extracted from the downloaded reference video. A frame of someone's copyrighted
# video is that copyrighted work just as much as the file it came from, and
# committing one to a PUBLIC repo redistributes it. Same rule as the video, so it
# gets the same treatment. Ours are named o_*.png under work/study/ours/ and are
# NOT matched -- keep them.
work/study/ref_*.png
work/**/ref_*.png

# Rendered output and per-segment renders.
work/assembly/
work3/assembly/
work3/segments/*/segment.mp4
work3/segments/*/_silent.mp4

# Debug frame dumps and contact sheets -- regenerable, and there are tens of
# thousands of them. work/segments alone held 25,040 PNGs (per-frame dumps from
# the first exoplanet build). These are DIAGNOSTIC OUTPUT, not references, but
# they are enormous and throwaway.
measure/
work3/measure/
work/segments/**/*.png
work/_preflight/
work/_scratch_g7verify/
work/_emissive_demo/
work/dbg_b*/
work/_diag*.png
work/_g[0-9]*.png
work/_sm*.png
work/test_*.png
work3/measure/_*.png
work3/lib/_dbg_*.png
work3/lib/_cmp_*.png
work3/lib/_test_*.png
*.log
!*.md

# Python bytecode and local env.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.env

# Editor / OS cruft.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/